    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:title>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Close-up, selective focus profile view of two young European Rabbits (Oryctolagus cuniculus) peeking out of their burrow. European rabbit or common rabbit (Oryctolagus cuniculus) is a species of rabbit native to southwestern Europe (Spain and Portugal) and northwest Africa (Morocco and Algeria). It has been widely introduced elsewhere, often with devastating effects on local biodiversity.</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
